# 🚦 Project 4 – Traffic Light Controller

## Objective

The objective of this project was to design a basic traffic light controller using an Arduino Uno, three LEDs, and timed state transitions.

This project builds on previous GPIO projects by introducing multiple outputs, sequencing, and function-based code organization.

---

## Background

A traffic light is a simple example of a finite state machine. The system cycles through a fixed sequence of states:

RED → GREEN → YELLOW → RED

Each state defines the complete output condition of the system. Only one LED should be active at a time.

